WEBVTT

00:09.280 --> 00:12.150
at the hands of the boy embraced by the Reaper.

00:13.280 --> 00:14.610
However,

00:14.610 --> 00:17.700
it was as if the blood spraying
from the Corpse was spreading.

00:18.410 --> 00:24.250
But it was the Lightless Realm that started to stir once again and attempted to expand its territory further.

00:26.420 --> 00:35.680
While mumbling, "Within the world of
shadow and mist is where true peace lies."

00:54.740 --> 01:03.080
The ink on today's graffiti runs

01:03.080 --> 01:14.090
A bicycle that has been abandoned awaits someone's return

01:14.090 --> 01:25.060
When we realized, it was up for us to choose if our existence is a replica or not

01:25.060 --> 01:29.440
Where is our proof?

01:29.440 --> 01:34.530
It's mankinds nature to come together

01:34.530 --> 01:39.570
Our love and bonds are things we can trust

01:39.570 --> 01:44.370
My sins are to be doubted

01:44.370 --> 01:50.710
The light I saw when you first held out your right hand

01:54.090 --> 01:59.550
We really are

02:08.060 --> 02:10.270
The Dark Metal

02:14.480 --> 02:19.070
Episode 14
Sounds of Regret

02:22.910 --> 02:24.120
This is Kamakura.

02:27.160 --> 02:28.660
And this here is Atsugi.

02:29.830 --> 02:33.250
It's speculated that these phenomena's in the Kanto region

02:33.250 --> 02:38.930
are the result of the metallic particles that were dispersed from the Lightless Realm.

02:38.930 --> 02:42.890
In other words, you at IX misjudged something.

02:42.890 --> 02:44.100
That can't be.

02:44.100 --> 02:46.020
We'll look into this starting now.

02:46.020 --> 02:51.020
It's pretty obvious that this is the result of a Gargouille member thoughtlessly attacking the Corpse.

02:51.020 --> 02:55.610
That may be true, but the commander was someone you dispatched.

02:55.610 --> 02:56.610
I'm Suzaki.

02:56.610 --> 02:57.650
I am terribly sorry.

02:58.440 --> 02:59.700
But regarding this case,

02:59.700 --> 03:04.950
it was something one of our pilots committed at his own discretion.

03:04.950 --> 03:08.080
We never expected something like this to happen at all.

03:08.080 --> 03:10.120
That's how things went, right, Natsuiri-kun?

03:10.120 --> 03:11.620
Who knows?

03:11.620 --> 03:15.590
That's probably the case since the pilot died.

03:15.590 --> 03:16.750
Wha—

03:20.090 --> 03:21.260
Akashi...

03:21.260 --> 03:24.970
Which is why it's meaningless to point fingers.

03:24.970 --> 03:25.890
Natsuiri!

03:26.470 --> 03:31.100
In any case, starting now,
all IX departments will follow our orders

03:31.100 --> 03:33.310
and will refrain from acting of their own accord.

03:34.810 --> 03:37.280
As for the newly developed version of the Vess...

03:37.280 --> 03:38.900
They're called MA-Vess, correct?

03:39.400 --> 03:41.360
These will also be placed under our management.

03:43.070 --> 03:47.790
We'll continue to look forward
to IX's work as a research facility.

03:48.240 --> 03:51.750
In any case, killing the Corpse was a fruit of your labors.

03:51.750 --> 03:55.000
Huh? Killing the Corpse?

03:56.630 --> 03:59.010
The Corpse! Did it die?

03:59.010 --> 04:00.840
That's what you folks said.

04:00.840 --> 04:04.550
No, we never said we killed it,

04:04.550 --> 04:07.560
but we did say we defeated it.

04:07.560 --> 04:11.810
In the first place, is the Corpse even an organism?

04:11.810 --> 04:13.190
That's what we're asking you!

04:13.600 --> 04:18.650
The Admonitions are biologically
dead as well, so even if you say kill...

04:18.650 --> 04:20.570
If you know something, then tell us!

04:20.570 --> 04:25.200
If we knew such a thing, we wouldn't be
going through all this trouble, would we?

04:25.910 --> 04:28.200
Oh, right. Maki Minashi-kun.

04:29.490 --> 04:35.000
You were able to bring back a piece of the Corpse's body, isn't that right?

04:35.000 --> 04:37.540
Yes. It was supposedly attached to the MA-Vess—

04:37.540 --> 04:39.420
Yes, that's enough.

04:42.050 --> 04:46.180
It's a bit frozen, so it's kinda hard to see.

04:46.180 --> 04:48.220
I can take it out,

04:48.220 --> 04:51.930
but if the metallic particles disperse,
all of you might turn into Necrometal.

04:52.980 --> 04:54.440
Whoops!

04:56.350 --> 04:58.770
That was dangerously close just now.

04:58.770 --> 05:03.570
Now, if we were to research the structural composition of the Corpse in here,

05:03.570 --> 05:08.820
there's a possiblity that we may find a clue to
prevent turning into Nectrometal or even curing it.

05:08.820 --> 05:11.540
Medicine? Can you make a remedy?

05:11.540 --> 05:13.540
The possibility is there.

05:14.000 --> 05:20.170
Tough this is only possible if the current condition where we can freely enter the Lightless Realm

05:20.170 --> 05:22.880
to do research remains untouched.

05:25.760 --> 05:26.880
Oh!

05:26.880 --> 05:28.260
I just remembered.

05:29.720 --> 05:35.520
Can the members of Team Gargouille—the ones I introduced to you at the start of this meeting—stand up?

05:38.850 --> 05:43.230
As you may already know, they are
the children that were spirited away.

05:43.230 --> 05:47.860
The miraculous children who lived to return from the Lightless Realm ten years ago.

05:47.860 --> 05:50.740
Though they look rather ordinary.

05:51.410 --> 05:53.200
"Children that were spirited away"?

05:54.000 --> 05:56.790
You may also know that they are Linkers—

05:56.790 --> 06:00.960
persons who posses the power of telepathy.

06:03.460 --> 06:07.970
Without said powers, it is impossible to pilot a MA-Vess.

06:07.970 --> 06:09.340
Is that true?

06:09.890 --> 06:10.800
Yes.

06:11.510 --> 06:12.930
Listen here!

06:12.930 --> 06:14.390
This is the key point!

06:14.390 --> 06:18.940
Aside from them, there is no other personnel
that can possibly investigate the Lightless Realm!

06:18.940 --> 06:25.230
And in order to maximize their
powers to their utmost potential, I...

06:25.690 --> 06:28.860
My intelligence is absolutely necessary.

06:28.860 --> 06:29.950
And furthermore,

06:29.950 --> 06:33.950
you cannot make me act via authority or orders.

06:34.660 --> 06:38.160
The only person who can order me around is myself.

06:47.760 --> 06:50.890
So Emiru's Ma-Vess has been repaired, right?

06:50.890 --> 06:52.970
Oh... Y-Yeah.

06:55.640 --> 06:57.730
He's mocking us!

06:57.730 --> 07:01.060
We're not even sure if Akashi is really dead!

07:01.810 --> 07:03.440
And what was that he said?

07:03.440 --> 07:05.270
"Spirited away children"...

07:05.270 --> 07:06.940
I've never heard or been called that!

07:06.940 --> 07:09.240
But that's one less question to worry about.

07:09.240 --> 07:13.120
The reason we were all gathered here was because of that.

07:13.120 --> 07:17.370
He said we returned from the Lightless Realm, but I don't remember anything about that.

07:18.450 --> 07:19.580
Mahmu.

07:21.580 --> 07:26.000
How much do you remember
from back when you were a kid?

07:27.340 --> 07:28.880
How much?

07:31.300 --> 07:33.090
You remember something?

07:33.090 --> 07:34.760
No, nothing at all.

07:34.760 --> 07:37.060
Don't you be hiding stuff at this point.

07:37.060 --> 07:39.680
If something came across your mind, then speak up, Mahmu.

07:40.520 --> 07:41.480
Well...

07:41.940 --> 07:46.610
I just thought of how I probably still have a story that I wrote back then.

07:46.610 --> 07:47.980
Probably?

07:47.980 --> 07:50.530
I don't remember when I actually wrote it.

07:51.820 --> 07:53.610
Are you serious?

07:53.610 --> 07:54.950
I want to see that.

07:54.950 --> 07:58.120
Oh, but it's just a story...

07:58.120 --> 07:59.700
Sorry to make you wait.

08:00.330 --> 08:02.960
Thanks for attending that meeting.

08:02.960 --> 08:05.750
Enough about that. Tell us now!

08:05.750 --> 08:08.170
What is this "children that were spirited away" stuff?

08:16.550 --> 08:18.010
It's just cola.

08:18.010 --> 08:21.390
I wouldn't bring my precious sample to a place like that!

08:22.520 --> 08:23.890
In any case,

08:23.890 --> 08:26.860
the Lightless Realm grows with each passing day,

08:27.270 --> 08:32.860
so there's a need to continue our
investigation with more effort than before.

08:33.650 --> 08:37.700
You're worried whether your
friends left inside are alive, right?

08:37.700 --> 08:39.910
The nerve of you... Damn you!

08:39.910 --> 08:44.330
Sadly, we gave up on the idea of
Isaku Heito's returning a while ago.

08:44.330 --> 08:46.460
So instead...

08:46.460 --> 08:48.460
If Heito's unavailable, then you're gonna use someone else.

08:48.460 --> 08:50.420
But I wonder, is it really that simple?

08:50.420 --> 08:52.300
Of course not.

08:52.300 --> 08:54.760
But there was one thing I overlooked.

08:54.760 --> 09:00.060
It was a compatibility issue I couldn't measure with just synchronicity.

09:00.060 --> 09:00.970
Compatibility?

09:00.970 --> 09:04.440
Emiru was rejecting him all the while.

09:04.440 --> 09:08.400
Yet still, Heito wrestled his way in with sheer force.

09:08.400 --> 09:10.020
How do I put this...

09:10.020 --> 09:13.820
It wasn't a resonance that resulted from mutual agreement.

09:13.820 --> 09:14.650
Impossible...

09:14.650 --> 09:16.160
And so...

09:16.160 --> 09:20.490
I was thinking... How about you pilot it instead?

09:21.740 --> 09:23.950
Mahmu.

09:25.540 --> 09:26.460
Me?

09:28.830 --> 09:29.590
Why?

09:29.590 --> 09:32.420
Minashi-kun already has Sasame-chan,

09:32.420 --> 09:35.930
and Iwato-kun and Raika-kun are extremely compatible.

09:35.930 --> 09:38.010
But that won't happen for a while.

09:38.010 --> 09:40.100
But for Mahmu to...

09:40.100 --> 09:41.890
It's impossible?

09:41.890 --> 09:45.560
Let's stop tiptoeing around her like some touchy subject.

09:46.390 --> 09:48.980
Though I understand that you would be worried about her.

09:48.980 --> 09:50.940
I'm sure she...

09:50.940 --> 09:52.690
I'll pilot it.

09:52.690 --> 09:53.780
Mahmu!

09:54.570 --> 09:55.950
I'll pilot it.

09:55.950 --> 09:57.530
That's good.

09:57.530 --> 09:59.200
That's very good, Mahmu!

09:59.200 --> 10:01.200
Then let's begin right away.

10:01.200 --> 10:03.120
Emiru is waiting!

10:05.870 --> 10:07.670
Boot sequence preparation at 90%.

10:12.550 --> 10:13.590
Emiru.

10:14.510 --> 10:16.130
Mahmu, are you doing okay?

10:16.130 --> 10:17.590
O-Oh, yes.

10:17.590 --> 10:19.510
Boot sequence preparation complete.

10:20.050 --> 10:21.220
Start it!

10:26.140 --> 10:28.730
Emiru, can you hear me?

10:29.900 --> 10:31.480
Resonance level is zero.

10:31.480 --> 10:34.400
The LIM's not booting up at all.

10:34.400 --> 10:38.070
They're both so cowardly... Just remove all the filters.

10:38.070 --> 10:39.610
But that's way to—

10:39.610 --> 10:40.530
Move aside.

10:40.530 --> 10:44.830
They're the type that won't link unless you force them to.

10:50.880 --> 10:59.050
I'm sorry... I'm sorry... I'm sorry...

11:04.640 --> 11:06.470
Mahmu! No, stop it!

11:10.850 --> 11:13.560
She lost consciousness.

11:13.560 --> 11:15.730
This matching is futile.

11:15.730 --> 11:17.530
Futile or not...

11:17.530 --> 11:23.740
She merely created an image of terror on her own
and was trembling from it just before she was linked.

11:27.490 --> 11:29.000
I got puke on me.

11:29.000 --> 11:30.710
Stay away, okay?

11:30.710 --> 11:31.710
That's harsh.

11:31.710 --> 11:33.500
I worked hard to carry her.

11:37.000 --> 11:40.970
Hey, if I end up a MA-Vess, you pilot it.

11:40.970 --> 11:42.180
What's with this all of a sudden?

11:42.180 --> 11:43.220
What do you mean?

11:44.010 --> 11:49.640
When Natsuiri said, "But that won't happen for a while,"

11:49.640 --> 11:53.100
he had this nasty grin on his face when he looked at us.

11:54.360 --> 11:56.480
He's expecting it to happen.

11:56.480 --> 11:58.610
Either for me or for you.

11:58.610 --> 12:01.030
He's expecting something disgusting.

12:01.030 --> 12:02.490
Can you put up with it?

12:04.070 --> 12:09.700
Back when I was a test pilot, I was pretty good at it.

12:09.700 --> 12:14.330
Forcefully pushing a gimmicky mech to do what I wanted.

12:14.330 --> 12:17.290
Are you fine being under my thumb like that?

12:18.090 --> 12:20.760
When you put it that way, it sounds really irritating.

12:21.340 --> 12:22.260
Right?

12:22.840 --> 12:26.640
I'm not gonna turn into a LIM, and I won't let you.

12:26.640 --> 12:29.310
Let's fight together as pilots.

12:29.310 --> 12:30.020
Forever.

12:36.190 --> 12:36.980
Raika...

12:36.980 --> 12:38.520
Wait, h-hold on...

12:38.520 --> 12:40.480
Our compatibility is good.

12:40.480 --> 12:43.200
I said to hold on... No!

12:43.200 --> 12:45.360
Sheesh! You'll get puke on me!

12:51.370 --> 12:52.750
What are you doing?

12:52.750 --> 12:54.290
You should be a good girl and rest.

12:55.250 --> 12:58.040
Is that the story you were talking about earlier?

12:59.380 --> 13:00.500
Y-Yeah.

13:08.300 --> 13:15.890
"When Mahsa yelled, 'The world is so horrible. Everyone should disappear!'"

13:15.890 --> 13:17.860
Hey, how do you read this?

13:17.860 --> 13:19.480
Blue empyrean.

13:19.480 --> 13:21.530
"From the far ends of the blue empyrean..."

13:22.320 --> 13:24.900
"...a catastrophe closes in."

13:24.900 --> 13:26.320
This is pretty good.

13:26.320 --> 13:27.450
It's tasteful.

13:27.450 --> 13:28.870
Though I don't quite get it.

13:28.870 --> 13:31.240
Don't force yourself to read it...

13:31.240 --> 13:35.250
This Mahsa person in the story is based on you, right?

13:35.250 --> 13:39.670
Both of your names are really similar, but the girl in
here is really dull since she does nothing but write stories.

13:40.460 --> 13:42.420
She is dull, isn't she?

13:42.420 --> 13:43.710
I think it's okay.

13:43.710 --> 13:46.970
By the way, why did you try piloting today?

13:47.590 --> 13:49.930
You were trying so hard to pilot Emiru's machine.

13:50.760 --> 13:53.470
I felt some pity for her.

13:53.470 --> 13:59.060
I thought that it would be better for me to pilot it than Heito-san forcing himself to.

14:00.360 --> 14:02.110
But apparently that wasn't so.

14:04.030 --> 14:07.240
I could only come up with scary images.

14:07.240 --> 14:09.280
Maybe she has a grudge against me after all.

14:11.490 --> 14:14.450
Why would Emiru have a grudge against you?

14:14.450 --> 14:15.450
Isn't it the other way around?

14:17.040 --> 14:19.540
Do you remember, Raika-san?

14:20.210 --> 14:26.420
When we went to look for the Reaper, I left Emiru behind and ran away.

14:27.050 --> 14:29.220
I left her all alone with Heito-san.

14:38.020 --> 14:39.770
This is horrible.

14:39.770 --> 14:41.020
It's all scratched out...

14:41.020 --> 14:41.730
Don't look at it!

14:44.110 --> 14:45.070
Mahmu?

14:45.730 --> 14:51.320
I wrote some terrible things
about Emiru in this notebook, so...

14:51.320 --> 14:54.620
But that's a pretty old notebook you got there.

14:59.160 --> 15:01.130
What was this one about?

15:10.510 --> 15:12.430
She wants to pilot it again?

15:13.180 --> 15:15.180
And she said it herself, did she?

15:15.180 --> 15:16.890
That's great news.

15:25.110 --> 15:28.400
Emiru, I want to be connected with you.

15:30.320 --> 15:33.450
Lowering shield rate to 70%.

15:38.620 --> 15:40.040
You're kidding...

15:40.040 --> 15:41.790
I'm back here again?

15:56.810 --> 15:57.850
Emiru...

15:57.850 --> 16:00.060
Emiru, I'm sorry.

16:00.060 --> 16:01.600
I won't leave you again—

16:11.610 --> 16:14.030
No... I can't run from this.

16:39.390 --> 16:41.230
I can't do this after all!

16:43.520 --> 16:45.690
I don't want to die, Mahmu...

16:45.690 --> 16:47.150
No!

16:51.070 --> 16:52.110
Don't come near me!

16:52.110 --> 16:53.570
Mahmu...

16:53.570 --> 16:56.280
No! Don't come near me! No!

16:56.740 --> 16:59.240
Resonance rate is rising.

16:59.240 --> 17:01.580
Currently at 22%.

17:01.580 --> 17:03.750
Oh, this may be better than our predictions.

17:05.080 --> 17:06.460
Mahmu...

17:11.840 --> 17:12.880
Emiru...

17:18.260 --> 17:22.220
This is a small forest that nobody else knows about.

17:22.980 --> 17:27.770
Nobody knows that nine children accidentally wandered into it.

17:28.310 --> 17:30.020
Mahsa was very unfortunate.

17:30.860 --> 17:35.530
The other eight have forgotten
about her, so she was always alone.

17:36.030 --> 17:38.370
But that didn't matter at all.

17:38.370 --> 17:39.490
Because...

17:39.490 --> 17:41.540
Because everything about the world was crap.

17:43.080 --> 17:48.080
She wished for the world to
become filled with unhappiness.

17:48.920 --> 17:51.000
She said "crap" in a fairy tale!

17:53.510 --> 17:54.880
What?

17:54.880 --> 17:57.430
You look like you're staring at a monster.

17:58.300 --> 17:59.390
So...

17:59.390 --> 18:01.810
What happens to that girl after that?

18:01.810 --> 18:05.350
Well, it's only a fairy tale...

18:05.350 --> 18:07.350
I like fairy tales.

18:07.350 --> 18:12.270
Like how a poor girl can become rich just because she had a glass slipper.

18:12.270 --> 18:13.730
Her dreams took her there.

18:14.860 --> 18:17.150
Hey, so what happens after?

18:17.150 --> 18:18.490
Leave me alone!

18:21.950 --> 18:23.910
Green light...

18:24.330 --> 18:25.580
...red light!

18:25.580 --> 18:27.120
Emiru moved!

18:27.120 --> 18:28.330
I didn't!

18:27.120 --> 18:28.330
Today, once again...

18:28.920 --> 18:29.830
Over here!

18:29.830 --> 18:32.340
Everyone was playing together happily.

18:32.340 --> 18:36.010
That's why Mahsa was unhappy again today.

18:36.010 --> 18:41.300
But the fact that she was alone was nothing really special.

18:41.300 --> 18:43.810
Hey, hey. Whatcha eating, Akashi?

18:44.260 --> 18:45.850
What is this?

18:45.850 --> 18:47.480
You don't know Umashi bars?

18:47.480 --> 18:50.020
It didn't matter to her at all that
the entire world was ignoring her...

18:52.560 --> 18:56.280
...because the world was crap after all.

18:58.240 --> 18:59.990
My notebook... Where's my notebook?

19:06.040 --> 19:06.910
Give it back!

19:13.670 --> 19:16.710
Oh, I found this on a tree stump.

19:16.710 --> 19:18.130
You're terrible!

19:18.130 --> 19:20.760
I told you to leave me alone.

19:20.760 --> 19:24.220
I had this feeling that I shouldn't when you act so miserable.

19:24.220 --> 19:26.180
I'm not acting miserable at all!

19:26.430 --> 19:27.930
You're acting miserable, aren't you?

19:29.230 --> 19:31.230
Deep down, you want others to butt in.

19:31.940 --> 19:33.310
I...

19:33.310 --> 19:37.480
You're lonely, and you desperately want to be noticed.

19:37.480 --> 19:39.650
But you act the lonely heroine!

19:39.650 --> 19:41.240
Isn't that what's crap?

19:41.240 --> 19:42.820
You're terrible...

19:42.820 --> 19:47.740
If you continue to fool your miserable self
by acting like that, you will never break out.

19:48.330 --> 19:51.250
You'll just go in circles around the same place over and over.

19:53.290 --> 19:56.920
You can never become happy that way.

19:58.590 --> 19:59.880
Emiru?

20:02.630 --> 20:04.720
I'm sorry about the notebook.

20:06.970 --> 20:09.140
I finally remembered...

20:10.520 --> 20:14.600
You were the one who wrote in
my notebook without permission.

20:15.650 --> 20:18.280
Mahsa wasn't just me...

20:25.030 --> 20:29.080
It didn't matter to her at all that
the entire world was ignoring her.

20:30.870 --> 20:32.830
But if just one person...

20:33.580 --> 20:38.000
If there was at least one person who would take the time to look at her,

20:38.750 --> 20:41.670
then perhaps the world would look better.

20:41.670 --> 20:43.720
That was what Mahsa thought.

20:46.390 --> 20:51.520
Emiru was trying to make the perpetually
unhappy Mahsa into someone who was happy.

20:53.520 --> 20:58.730
We expressed it in different ways,
but we were fundamentally the same.

20:59.400 --> 21:03.700
Loneliness was too painful for both myself and Emiru.

21:04.650 --> 21:08.070
All we wanted was happiness.

21:08.830 --> 21:10.160
Emiru...

21:15.580 --> 21:18.040
Mahmu...

21:23.300 --> 21:24.260
I understand...

21:25.260 --> 21:28.800
I can feel what your heart says, Emiru...

21:29.260 --> 21:33.430
Emiru, your feelings aren't dead yet!

21:34.480 --> 21:36.770
They're not dead at all!

21:37.520 --> 21:39.020
I'll be here with you.

21:40.480 --> 21:44.610
I can be here with you, right, Emiru?

21:53.160 --> 21:55.160
Synchronization rate is rising.

21:55.160 --> 21:56.410
Yes, yes, here it is!

21:57.580 --> 21:59.500
The LIM booted up!

22:08.300 --> 22:12.890
If there was at least one person who would take the time to look at her,

22:13.600 --> 22:15.810
then perhaps the world would look better.

22:17.770 --> 22:19.480
Emiru was still alive.

22:20.190 --> 22:23.570
It was a miracle caused by her strong will.

22:24.150 --> 22:27.990
The will to live—to live on, and fight once again

22:28.610 --> 22:32.740
for the sake of happiness,
instead of for the sake of revenge.

22:56.390 --> 23:00.440
You lose your mind, you crash; a nervous breakdown

23:00.440 --> 23:05.190
You feel an urge inside, you crush; there's no escape now

23:05.190 --> 23:10.070
You try to change your life, you jump another let down

23:10.070 --> 23:12.660
But then you hear a voice inside

23:12.660 --> 23:15.950
You gotta open up your vision and see the life bestowed on you

23:15.950 --> 23:18.540
Blinded by reality

23:18.540 --> 23:20.710
Broken ideology

23:20.710 --> 23:23.250
Heart in captivity

23:23.250 --> 23:25.590
Hold on, exceeding the borders within

23:25.590 --> 23:28.090
Seize your capability

23:28.090 --> 23:30.470
Endless possibility

23:30.470 --> 23:32.800
Find your individuality

23:32.890 --> 23:35.010
Take pride; let the chase begin

23:35.010 --> 23:37.680
Don't tell me what direction you think I should take

23:37.680 --> 23:39.480
I know now to find the way

23:39.480 --> 23:42.480
Don’t tell me that this sable is for my own sake

23:42.480 --> 23:44.020
Here's what I’ve got to say

23:44.020 --> 23:47.280
Don't tell me to believe the decisions you make

23:47.280 --> 23:49.490
Facing a new day

23:49.490 --> 23:51.480
So open up your blinded eyes

23:51.480 --> 23:54.490
Stop living a lie and start living your life

23:54.490 --> 23:56.830
My way or no way

23:56.830 --> 23:59.290
Today you’re falling away

24:05.040 --> 24:10.050
Episode 15

24:05.040 --> 24:10.050
Vacant Heart of Morning Gray
